\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two distinct temporal arcs}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The [torus reflections](fdip-007M) assume a temporal period
of at least #{4}. A cellular circle can instead have two vertices
and two distinct arcs joining them. Reversing time exchanges the
vertices and reverses each arc. Which connection data and which
field locations remain fixed by that operation?}
